<dtcname>A/B ECU Communication Stop Mode</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000OEI00PX_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000D800000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Suspected Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A/B ECU Communication Stop Mode</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle">
<ptxt>'Airbag' is not displayed on the TaSCAN [CAN Bus Connected ECU Check] screen</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU) branch line open circuit or connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU) power supply system</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU) internal malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000OEI00PX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000D900000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162435J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000OEI00PX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DA00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When measuring the resistance of the CAN bus, turn the IG OFF, confirm that warning functions such as the key reminder warning system are not operating, and leave the vehicle for 1 minutes or more without operating the key or switches or opening/closing the doors before starting measurement. If it is necessary to open a door during inspection, open it beforehand.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When inspecting each connector, before disconnecting it, push the connector case in the connecting direction and check that the connector is not loose or disconnected.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When disconnecting a connector, check that the connector terminals and connector case are free of damage, deformation, corrosion, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000OEI00PX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000OEI00PX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DB00000">
<testtitle>CAN Bus Open Circuit Inspection (A/B ECU Branch Line)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF and disconnect the vehicle harness connector 1 of the airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU) from the airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C147881J06" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the vehicle harness connector of the airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU).</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.93in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.11in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1-13(CANH) - 1-22(CANL)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>54 to 69Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000OEI00PX_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000OEI00PX_04_0003" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000OEI00PX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DC00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness (ECU Power Source System)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance and voltage between each terminal of the airbag sensor assembly CTR (A/B ECU) vehicle harness connector and body ground.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C147881J05" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.93in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.12in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1-25 (E1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1-26 (E2) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Voltage</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.92in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1-21 (IG2) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000OEI00PX_04_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000OEI00PX_04_0004" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
